WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.800
Matthew Perry had the type of success&nbsp;
that most can only dream of — but it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:09.200
also came with a cost. From numerous&nbsp;
hospitalizations to the many years he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:14.320
spent battling his addiction, Perry's&nbsp;
personal life was far from perfect.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:19.680
Matthew Perry was raised in Ottawa, Canada, and&nbsp;
his parents were significant figures. His father,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.720
John Bennett Perry, was an American actor best&nbsp;
recognized for minor roles in films like "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.960
Legend of the Lone Ranger." Meanwhile,&nbsp;
Perry's mother, Suzanne Marie Morrison,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:33.760
was a former beauty queen who served as press&nbsp;
secretary to the country's Prime Minister.

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:38.120
"They're both people that take over&nbsp;
a room, you know, when they come in."

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:42.840
Unfortunately, the pair separated before&nbsp;
their son reached his first birthday. Perry's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:47.960
mother would find a new partner in celebrated&nbsp;
"Dateline" correspondent Keith Morrison. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:51.920
the young performer admitted that he didn't&nbsp;
see much of them while he was growing up. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:56.800
his 2022 memoir, "Friends, Lovers, and&nbsp;
the Big Terrible Thing," Perry wrote:

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.880
"I spent a great deal of time alone."

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:02.280
Even more tragically, when it came&nbsp;
to seeing his father, Perry wrote,
 &nbsp;

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:06.480
"I saw his face more often on TV or&nbsp;
in magazines than I did in reality."

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:11.720
Perry also admitted that he started misbehaving&nbsp;
at an early age. By the age of 10, he was smoking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:17.200
and stealing money. Meanwhile, Perry admitted&nbsp;
to having his first taste of alcohol at 14.
 &nbsp;

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.240
It may come as a surprise that before Perry&nbsp;
became an actor, he had his sights set on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:26.160
a tennis career. The actor first hit the court&nbsp;
when he was 4 years old. Training nearly 10 hours&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:31.760
a day by age 13, he ranked among the best for&nbsp;
juniors in his home country of Canada. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:35.960
when Perry moved in with his father in&nbsp;
California the reality of a sports career&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:40.480
seemed much more daunting. He explained&nbsp;
in a 2012 interview with Men's Health:

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:44.680
"I was a very good tennis player in Ottawa,&nbsp;
Canada — nationally ranked when I was, like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:48.720
13. Then I moved to Los Angeles&nbsp;
when I was 15, and everyone in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.520
L.A. just killed me. I was pretty great&nbsp;
in Canada. Not so much in Los Angeles."

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:56.880
Thankfully, the young star had a&nbsp;
backup plan. He told Men's Health:

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:00.960
"I realized I wouldn't be playing tennis for&nbsp;
a living, so I went for acting. Are tennis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:04.160
and acting alike? I don't know.&nbsp;
They're both very mental games."

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:08.080
While his career ultimately went in a different&nbsp;
direction, tennis remained a passion for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:14.360
the actor as his last public appearance was&nbsp;
reportedly at the 2023 French Open in Paris.
 &nbsp;

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:18.200
Matthew Perry openly expressed that the&nbsp;
most significant demon of his life was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:22.360
his addiction struggles. His memoirs'&nbsp;
release just one year before his passing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:25.920
illuminated many of the challenges&nbsp;
that the actor faced. He described&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:30.160
himself as an alcoholic since he first&nbsp;
started drinking as a teenager. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:34.400
his addictions overtook his life after he&nbsp;
was prescribed painkillers following a jet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:40.200
ski accident in 1997, resulting in his first&nbsp;
stay at a rehabilitation clinic the same year.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:45.640
By 2000, Perry's drinking led to him being&nbsp;
hospitalized with pancreatitis. That same year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:50.960
he crashed his Porsche into the steps of his&nbsp;
Hollywood home. In a 2002 interview with People,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:55.640
the actor described the amount of drugs and&nbsp;
alcohol he was consuming at the time. He told the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.640 --> 00:03:02.160
outlet that he'd ingest as many as "55 Vicodin" a&nbsp;
day while drinking upwards of "a quart of vodka."

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:09.160
"I had to wake up and realize that I needed to&nbsp;
get 55 of them or I was going to be real sick."

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:12.960
In a separate 2022 interview&nbsp;
with People, Perry admitted,

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:16.840
"I didn't know how to stop. If the&nbsp;
police came over to my house and said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:20.520
'If you drink tonight, we're going to&nbsp;
take you to jail,' I'd start packing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:24.120
I couldn't stop because the disease&nbsp;
and the addiction is progressive. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:26.813
it gets worse and worse as you grow older."

00:03:26.813 --> 00:03:29.081
Matthew Perry's addiction problems ultimately 

00:03:29.081 --> 00:03:34.600
collided with his acting career. Perry landed the&nbsp;
role of Chandler Bing when he was 24 years old,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:38.800
just as his addiction was truly beginning&nbsp;
to take the reins. He told People:

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:44.640
"I could handle it, kind of. But by the time I was&nbsp;
34, I was really entrenched in a lot of trouble."

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.400
While appearing on BBC Radio&nbsp;
2 in 2016, he was questioned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:52.080
on his least favorite episode from&nbsp;
"Friends," and he candidly replied,

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:54.920
"I think the answer is I don't&nbsp;
remember three years of it."

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:59.640
He went on to admit that Season 3 to Season&nbsp;
6 were blurred in his memories. The actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:03.200
struggled to look back at his time on&nbsp;
the beloved sitcom as it was equally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:07.640
one of the most challenging eras of his&nbsp;
life. He told Tom Power in an interview:

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:11.880
"I can't watch the show, because I was&nbsp;
brutally thin and being beaten down so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:16.120
badly by the disease. I could tell season&nbsp;
by season by how I looked, and I don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:18.934
think anybody else can, but I certainly could."

00:04:18.934 --> 00:04:21.779
As Perry's struggles with addiction intensified, 

00:04:21.779 --> 00:04:26.520
he worried about disappointing his co-stars.&nbsp;
The actor said in an ABC News interview:

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:29.760
"I made a rule that I would never&nbsp;
drink or take anything at work. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:33.560
I would show up blindly hung over.&nbsp;
I thought I was hiding it so well."

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:37.400
Unfortunately, the five other prominent&nbsp;
"Friends" were each affected by Perry's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:41.560
struggles at one point or another.&nbsp;
Lisa Kudrow told the New York Times:

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:44.960
"When Matthew was sick, it was&nbsp;
not fun. We were just hopelessly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:47.560
standing on the sidelines. We were hurting a lot."

00:04:47.560 --> 00:04:50.880
Meanwhile, Matt LeBlanc also admitted&nbsp;
to People that he tried to help his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:55.320
onscreen roommate but ultimately felt like&nbsp;
there was little he could do. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:59.640
it was Jennifer Anniston whom Perry&nbsp;
praised in his ABC interview, saying,

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:06.280
"She was the one that reached out the most.&nbsp;
You know, I'm really grateful to her for that."

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:09.120
Perry conceded that he would not&nbsp;
have made it through 10 seasons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:11.600
without his castmates, writing in his memoir,

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:15.600
"They were patient. It's like penguins.&nbsp;
Penguins, in nature, when one is sick,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:20.320
or when one is very injured, the other penguins&nbsp;
surround it and prop it up. They walk around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:25.120
it until that penguin can walk on its own.&nbsp;
That's kind of what the cast did for me."
 &nbsp;

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:27.840
Perry had a lifelong grudge&nbsp;
match with his addiction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:31.200
One of his biggest realizations came&nbsp;
when he put the numbers down for how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:35.160
much he has invested into getting&nbsp;
clean. He told the New York Times:

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:39.120
"I've probably spent $9 million or&nbsp;
something trying to get sober. It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:41.560
still a day-to-day process of getting better."

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:44.520
In addition to the time and&nbsp;
effort he put into sobriety,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:50.000
Perry also did his part to give back. In 2013,&nbsp;
he opened the doors of his Malibu beach house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:55.240
transitioning it into a dedicated sober living&nbsp;
facility for men suffering from addiction.

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:57.040
"If somebody comes up to me and says,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.040 --> 00:06:02.360
'I can't stop drinking. Can you help me?'&nbsp;
I can say yes and follow up and do it."

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:07.120
The aptly named Perry House was eventually&nbsp;
sold in 2015 because of the high operating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:11.480
costs of living in Malibu. However, Perry&nbsp;
continued to take significant pride in being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:16.040
able to help those who have suffered the same&nbsp;
hurdles as himself. He told People magazine:

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:19.960
"When I die, I'd like 'Friends' to&nbsp;
be listed behind helping people."

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:22.240
After decades of pushing his health to the brink,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:27.640
the substance use caught up with Matthew Perry&nbsp;
in 2018. The actor suffered a gastrointestinal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.640 --> 00:06:32.680
perforation and narrowly survived the&nbsp;
traumatic event. He told People in 2022;

00:06:32.680 --> 00:06:36.560
"The doctors told my family that I had a&nbsp;
two percent chance to live. I was put on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:40.240
a thing called an ECMO machine, which&nbsp;
does all the breathing for your heart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:43.840
and your lungs. And that's called&nbsp;
a Hail Mary. No one survives that."

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:46.080
Perry revealed that the life-threatening situation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:50.440
put him in a coma for two weeks followed&nbsp;
by a five-month hospital stay. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:55.480
the close call had lasting implications on his&nbsp;
life. He had over a dozen surgeries and carried&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.480 --> 00:07:00.120
a colostomy bag for nine months as a result&nbsp;
of his health complications. He recalled:

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:03.520
"My therapist said, 'The next time&nbsp;
you think about taking Oxycontin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:06.760
just think about having a colostomy&nbsp;
bag for the rest of your life.' A&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:11.200
little window opened and I crawled through&nbsp;
it and I no longer want Oxycontin anymore."

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:14.480
Undoubtedly, Perry counted his&nbsp;
blessings and used his second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:16.600
chance at life to complete&nbsp;
his memoirs. He told People:

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:19.120
"There were five people put on an ECMO machine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:23.280
that night and the other&nbsp;
four died and I survived."

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:27.120
Many of the details of Matthew Perry's life&nbsp;
have only become available thanks to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:30.840
actor's 2022 memoir. However,&nbsp;
when the book was published,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:35.480
Perry received heavy backlash from fans and&nbsp;
celebrities alike for taking punches at one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:39.840
of Hollywood's most beloved figures:&nbsp;
Keanu Reeves. Perry wrote in the book:

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:42.120
"Why is it that the original thinkers like River&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:46.160
Phoenix and Heath Ledger die, but&nbsp;
Keanu Reeves still walks among us?"

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:50.040
By all accounts, the "Friends" actor had never&nbsp;
professionally crossed paths with the "Matrix"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:55.400
star, making the name drop more confusing. In&nbsp;
the wake of the one-sided feud, many celebrities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.400 --> 00:08:00.360
vocalized their defense for Reeves. Billy Baldwin&nbsp;
said in a post on X, formerly known as Twitter,

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:03.480
"In a world full of Matthew&nbsp;
Perry's ... be a Keanu Reeves."

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:05.080
Following the negative reaction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:08.960
Perry was quick to apologize. The&nbsp;
actor said in a statement to Deadline:

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:14.000
"I'm actually a big fan of Keanu. I just&nbsp;
chose a random name, my mistake. I apologize.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:16.273
I should have used my own name instead."

00:08:16.273 --> 00:08:18.061
Throughout his life, Matthew Perry dated 

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:22.120
some of the biggest actresses in Hollywood.&nbsp;
Some of the high-profile women that crossed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:26.480
paths with the actor included Julia&nbsp;
Roberts and Gwyneth Paltrow. Sadly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:31.200
despite rubbing elbows with some of the most elite&nbsp;
bachelorettes, Perry never held down a committed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:36.160
relationship for long. While talking about his&nbsp;
past romantic life, Perry wrote in his book,

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:41.160
"I need love but I don't trust it. If I drop my&nbsp;
game like Chandler and show you who I really am&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:45.520
you might notice me — but worse you might notice&nbsp;
me and might leave me, and I can't have that."

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:47.960
On one of his most heartbreaking&nbsp;
breakups, he wrote,

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:53.360
"I was broken, bent, unlovable. So instead&nbsp;
of facing the inevitable agony of losing her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:56.880
I broke up with the beautiful&nbsp;
and brilliant Julia Roberts."

00:08:56.880 --> 00:08:58.920
"Are you dating this Matthew Perry guy?"

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:01.160
"I am dating this Matthew Perry guy."

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:05.240
The "Friends" star seemed to have finally found&nbsp;
love when he got engaged to Molly Hurwitz in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.240 --> 00:09:10.880
2020. However, the pair called off the wedding&nbsp;
a few months later, with Perry telling People,

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:14.280
"Sometimes things just don't work&nbsp;
out and this is one of them."
 &nbsp;

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:17.480
With all the tribulations that Matthew&nbsp;
Perry faced throughout his life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:22.760
the actor had seemingly gotten himself back on a&nbsp;
healthy track. While promoting his book in 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:26.720
he boasted a clean lifestyle. In his&nbsp;
interview with People, he even joked,

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:30.680
"I'm pretty healthy now. I've got to not go&nbsp;
to the gym much more because I don't want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:34.520
to only be able to play superheroes. But&nbsp;
no, I'm a pretty healthy guy right now."

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:37.560
With the worst seemingly&nbsp;
behind the beloved sitcom star,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:43.360
it was extra shocking when it was revealed on&nbsp;
October 28, 2023 that Perry had died from an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.360 --> 00:09:47.480
apparent drowning in a hot tub. Perry's&nbsp;
family wrote in a statement to People:

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:51.640
"We are heartbroken by the tragic loss&nbsp;
of our beloved son and brother. Matthew&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.640 --> 00:09:55.600
brought so much joy to the world,&nbsp;
both as an actor and a friend."

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:58.920
Additionally, they sent a message&nbsp;
to Perry's fans across the globe:

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:03.440
"You all meant so much to him and we&nbsp;
appreciate the tremendous outpouring of love."

